"entity": {
"name": "Jefferson Capital, Inc.",
"description": "Jefferson Capital, Inc. is a holding company, which engages in purchasing and managing charge-off and insolvency of consumer accounts. It operates two main primary lines of business, which includes Distressed and Insolvency segments. The Distressed segment represents the purchase, collection, and servicing collection of nonperforming consumer loans. The Insolvency segment consists of the purchasing and servicing of financial assets of consumers who have entered bankruptcy through Chapter 7 or 13 of the U.S. Bankruptcy Code in the United States, consumer proposal, credit counseling, or bankruptcy in Canada and the United Kingdom. The firm manages the following geographical segments: the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom, and Latin America. The company was founded by David M. Burton in 2002 and is headquartered in Minneapolis, MN.",
"rbics_econ": "Finance",
